hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16452","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Hisham ibn Urwa narrated to me, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Umayya al-Makhzumi, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, praying in the house of Umm Salama, wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in a single garment wrapped in it, with nothing else upon him."
"16453","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, that he said: Abdullah ibn Abi Umayya informed me that he saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, praying in the house of Umm Salama in a garment wrapped in it, with its ends crossed."
